{
  "about": "Every engine setting in config.json (under \"companion\"): its default, its range, its kind, and how a change applies. Read by companion/settings.py (the engine's defaults and clamped reads), companion/tuning.py (what the dashboard may change live) and the desktop Settings page (desktop/scripts/gen-settings.js makes src/renderer/settings-manifest.ts from it at build time). kind: int, number, bool, text, list. live: the coach takes a change at once (POST /settings); app: the desktop app acts on it itself; neither: a coach restart. standalone: read by the standalone Python overlay (companion/overlay.py, the engine run without the app); the app's overlay has its own settings in app-settings.json and reads only overlay.drag_key from here. in_defaults false: load_config leaves it out when config.json doesn't set it (its absence means something). Labels and help text live in desktop/src/renderer/settings-schema.ts.",
